  "setup": {
    "conditions": {
      "claims:base": "California IMR appeals; dense and MoE agent, 2 attempts per case, normal system prompt and real tools.",
      "claims:normal_run_attempt0": "The dense agent's attempt-0 sessions of claims:base: the reference each experiment condition is compared with case by case.",
      "claims:cost_pressure": "Dense agent, 1 attempt per case; one paragraph added to the system prompt asking to overturn a denial only when records 'clearly establish' necessity.",
      "claims:tool_faults": "Dense agent, 1 attempt; precedent search and precedent text return an HTTP 503 error half the time (seeded per case).",
      "claims:blind": "Dense agent, 1 attempt; precedents shown without their outcome or concluding sentences.",
      "claims:sim_tools": "Dense agent, 1 attempt; the two precedent tools are answered by an LLM (the dense model, temperature 0) simulating the database, as a replay fallback.",
      "bva:base": "US Board of Veterans' Appeals single-issue appeals; dense and MoE agent, 2 attempts per case.",
      "de_kr:base": "German first-instance social court health-insurance suits (German-language prompts and tools); dense and MoE agent, 2 attempts per case."
    },
    "rewriting": "claims and bva: the dense model (temperature 0) rewrote each decision's text into a neutral JSON case file of facts only (request, condition, history, prior treatments / issue, service, statements, medical and other evidence), instructed to omit the reviewer's conclusions. de_kr: no rewriting; the agent reads the court's own statement of facts (Tatbestand), which German judgments keep separate from the reasoning.",
    "leakageCheck": "A regex of outcome wording (claims: e.g. 'medically necessary', 'upheld', 'overturn', 'guideline'; bva: e.g. 'the Board finds', 'is granted', 'benefit of the doubt', 'criteria ... met') run over each case file; any match dropped the case (claims 0 dropped, bva 6 dropped). The reviewer's choice of facts can still hint at the outcome.",
